Z||000005||sqoach||02-14-2001||05:53 PM||||that's a pretty good site lisa. just a little limited to selection, but not too bad.<P>anthony (i'm assuming that's your name) i just re-read your first post a little better. when you asked if pioneer is worth the $99. i thought you were talking about a pioneer sub. my bad.<BR>i've heard from a lot of people that those pioneer 4x10s put out some decent bass. it just all depends on how much bass you want.||||reg||1
Z||000006||anthony_86gt||02-14-2001||05:56 PM||||Do i really need an amp??  im on a budget here tho.  i have a sony xplod cd player at 50x4.  and how much would it cost for an amp and hook up??  i only need 1 8" sub. which amp should i get?<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000007||sqoach||02-14-2001||06:22 PM||||when hooking up a sub, an amp is pretty much required. (in most cases) what's the power rating on your sub? (rms and peak power) what brand is it? ohms?<BR>how do you have it hooked up right now?<P>if you're on a pretty tight budget, maybe you should buy a good set of 4x10s. the bass isn't too bad.<BR>||||reg||1
